14.  Policies that put one political agency in charge of the means of 
communication have not historically been friendly to open inquiry and 
communication, because, even in the best case, that agency becomes 
responsible for what should, properly, be a matter of distributed 
responsibility, and acts more restrictively than would the varied set of 
distributed responsible agents.

